--

COMMENT ON COLUMN public.app_settings.sms_offer_enabled IS 'Florist offer SMS (dashboard/lib/reachoutSend.ts::sendOffer). Off = the offer still goes out via email + push; the atomic claim/status update are unaffected. Defaults FALSE (ships dark).';


--

--

COMMENT ON COLUMN public.app_settings.sms_recruiting_enabled IS 'Florist recruiting/outreach SMS (dashboard/app/api/outreach/send/route.ts, channel=sms). Off = an SMS batch is skipped and logged, nothing is sent. Defaults FALSE (ships dark).';


--

--

COMMENT ON COLUMN public.app_settings.hold_delivery_payouts IS 'Operator override: put the 30% delivery leg back in the CX approval queue by hand. Default false — a delivered photo releases the 30%, and the AI photo check (dashboard/lib/payoutHold.ts) holds it only on a review/fail verdict. Not read for the 70% accept leg.';


--

--

COMMENT ON COLUMN public.app_settings.active_order_tags IS 'Opt-in tag allow-list gating order matching. Empty = match/show every order (default, backward-compatible). Non-empty = only orders whose Shopify tags intersect this set are matched and shown by default; others are ingested but left at status ''received''.';


--

--

COMMENT ON COLUMN public.app_settings.email_offer_enabled IS 'Florist offer email (dashboard/lib/reachoutSend.ts::sendOffer). Off = the offer still goes out via push only; the atomic claim/status update are unaffected.';


--

--

COMMENT ON COLUMN public.app_settings.email_client_assigned_enabled IS 'Client "order assigned" notice (dashboard/lib/clientComms.ts::notifyClient, kind=assigned). Off = skipped, and the per-(order,kind) idempotency claim is NOT taken, so turning it back on still allows one send.';


--

--

COMMENT ON COLUMN public.app_settings.email_client_on_the_way_enabled IS 'Client "on the way" notice (dashboard/lib/clientComms.ts::notifyClient, kind=on_the_way). Same off-semantics as email_client_assigned_enabled.';


--

--

COMMENT ON COLUMN public.app_settings.email_client_delivered_enabled IS 'Client "delivered" notice (dashboard/lib/clientComms.ts::notifyClient, kind=delivered). Same off-semantics as email_client_assigned_enabled.';


--

--

COMMENT ON COLUMN public.app_settings.email_issue_to_florist_enabled IS 'Email to the florist when CX replies/resolves an issue (dashboard/lib/issueComms.ts::notifyFloristOfIssue). Off = skipped; the issue thread itself is unaffected.';


--

--

COMMENT ON COLUMN public.app_settings.email_issue_to_cx_enabled IS 'Email to CX/ops when a florist opens/replies to an issue (dashboard/lib/issueComms.ts::notifyCxOfIssue). Off = skipped; the issue thread itself is unaffected.';


--

--

COMMENT ON COLUMN public.app_settings.email_cx_alert_enabled IS 'CX SLA breach alert email (dashboard/lib/cxAlerts.ts::sweepCxAlerts). This is a safety alert for stuck orders/money — leave on unless testing. Off only stops the EMAIL leg; the staff web-push still fires.';


--

--

COMMENT ON COLUMN public.app_settings.email_recruiting_enabled IS 'Florist recruiting/outreach emails (dashboard/app/api/outreach/send/route.ts). Off = the whole batch is skipped and logged, nothing is sent.';


--

--

COMMENT ON COLUMN public.app_settings.florist_support_email IS 'Support contact shown in the florist order-offer email footer (Settings). Null falls back to the hardcoded default in dashboard/lib/reachoutSend.ts.';


--

--

COMMENT ON COLUMN public.app_settings.stats_chat_model IS 'OpenRouter model slug used by the Statistics page LLM chat (app/api/stats/chat/route.ts). Editable from Settings.';


--

--

COMMENT ON COLUMN public.app_settings.test_shop_matching IS 'How automatic matching treats florists.is_test_shop: ''exclude'' (default, test shops never receive real orders) or ''only'' (matching routes exclusively to test shops — a testing mode that strands non-test orders in CX).';


--

--

COMMENT ON COLUMN public.app_settings.cold_offer_enabled IS 'Master switch for offering real orders to shops outside the network. FALSE by default. Even when on, lib/waves.ts only auto-sends a cold offer in workflow_mode=auto; in semi it still files an order_approvals row, which is where cold offers should live until the numbers are trusted.';


--

--

COMMENT ON COLUMN public.app_settings.cold_offer_max_payout_eur IS 'A cold offer is only eligible below this payout. The single cheapest risk control here: it bounds the worst case before any other machinery is involved.';


--

--

COMMENT ON COLUMN public.app_settings.cold_offer_auto_payout_cap_eur IS 'Above this, a provisional shop''s 70% accept leg is parked as payouts.status=''held'' (which already surfaces on /cx as "approve release") rather than issued unattended. The honest compromise between "70% up front" and "we have never met you".';


--

--

COMMENT ON COLUMN public.app_settings.message_voice IS 'kind -> "branded"|"plain". Keys are the same `kind` strings lib/communications.ts logs (offer, recruit.t1 … recruit.co2, persona_reply). Missing key or unrecognised value resolves to "branded" (lib/messageVoice.ts::voiceForKind, fail-open). A per-sequence-step override lives in lib/sequences/definitions.ts and WINS over this map — see resolveVoice.';


--

--

COMMENT ON COLUMN public.app_settings.sequence_enabled IS 'Master switch for the outreach funnel (lib/sequences/tick.ts). Defaults FALSE — the engine ships dark and is turned on deliberately, per the same fail-closed reasoning as the SMS toggles.';


--

--

COMMENT ON COLUMN public.app_settings.sequence_daily_send_cap IS 'Recruiting sends allowed per UTC day, counted across the tick''s own steps and the manual /discovery send. NULL = NO LIMIT (send everything due). 0 = send nothing, the kill switch — deliberately NOT the same as NULL. A positive number is the blast-radius guard it always was: a scheduling bug cannot empty the prospect list into one afternoon. See dashboard/lib/sequences/tick.ts.';


--

--

COMMENT ON COLUMN public.app_settings.voice_record_by_country IS 'ISO alpha-2 -> boolean override for audio recording, so a market can be switched off without a deploy and without stopping calls elsewhere. Read by lib/voice/recordingPolicy.ts, which treats an unparseable value as "do not record" — the safe direction.';


--

--

COMMENT ON COLUMN public.app_settings.voice_retention_days IS 'How long a recording and transcript are kept. GDPR Art. 5(1)(e): personal data may not be kept longer than necessary, and "forever" is never a defensible answer for a recording of somebody''s voice.';


--

--

COMMENT ON COLUMN public.app_settings.email_accept_confirm_enabled IS 'Florist "thank you for accepting" email (dashboard/lib/acceptComms.ts::notifyFloristOfAccept). Off = skipped and logged; the accept, the 70% payout leg and the client notice are unaffected.';


--

--

COMMENT ON COLUMN public.app_settings.sms_accept_confirm_enabled IS 'Florist "thank you for accepting" SMS (same send site). FAILS CLOSED like every sms_* toggle: only an explicit true sends. Off = the email leg still goes out.';


--

--

COMMENT ON COLUMN public.app_settings.florist_chat_enabled IS 'Whether the florist support chat (OrderChat) renders on an order page at all. Off hides the launcher and panel entirely. Independent of support_agent_enabled, which only gates the AI auto-reply once the chat is open.';


--

--

COMMENT ON COLUMN public.app_settings.cx_agent_max_auto_turns IS 'Hard ceiling on consecutive AI replies with no human involved. This — together with escalating whole INTENT CATEGORIES (pricing, legal, complaint, asked-for-a-human) before the text is even examined — is what actually bounds this feature. The text-matching guards are backstops.';


--

--

COMMENT ON COLUMN public.app_settings.support_agent_enabled IS 'Whether the order-aware support agent may answer a joined florist unattended. Ships false. cx_agent_min_confidence / cx_agent_max_auto_turns / cx_agent_model are shared with the recruiting agent deliberately — they are properties of how much we trust an unattended model, not of who it is writing to.';


--

--

COMMENT ON COLUMN public.app_settings.sequence_auto_enrol_scraped IS 'Opt-in: newly ingested shops (lifecycle_stage=found, with an email, ingested within the lookback window) are enrolled in recruit_cold automatically by the sequence tick. FALSE by default. No effect unless sequence_enabled is also on; the daily send cap still applies.';


--

--

COMMENT ON COLUMN public.app_settings.match_max_waves IS 'Hard ceiling on offer waves per order. Each wave refills up to match_top_n fresh candidates, so the most shops an order can be offered to unattended is match_max_waves × match_top_n. Reaching it escalates with reason wave_ceiling — untried shops may remain, which is why the CX desk offers "keep going" rather than only "place by hand". 1 = the pre-refill behavior (one wave, then escalate).';


--

--

COMMENT ON COLUMN public.app_settings.cx_reserve_hours IS 'Margin before delivery reserved for a human. The wave engine will not start an offer whose response window would end later than delivery_at minus this, escalating with reason out_of_time instead — so CX inherits the order while there is still time to place it. Orders with no delivery_at are bounded by match_max_waves alone.';


--

--

COMMENT ON COLUMN public.app_settings.call_back_gap_rush_min IS 'Minutes to wait before offering the same shop again after an unanswered call, for a delivery within 6h. Tiers mirror offer_window_*_min.';


--

--

COMMENT ON COLUMN public.app_settings.operator_view IS 'true = non-admin staff get the short sidebar (see OPERATOR_HIDDEN in components/shell/StaffShell.tsx). Hides links only; every route keeps its own role gate, so this is a decluttering setting and NOT an access control.';


--

--

COMMENT ON COLUMN public.app_settings.offer_short_variant_enabled IS 'false = every offer email uses the full opening, even for a shop that accepted recently. Read in lib/offerVars.ts where the variant is chosen; the offer itself is never suppressed by this.';


--

--

COMMENT ON COLUMN public.app_settings.sequence_auto_enrol_countries IS 'Country allow-list for the auto-enrol sweep, using the codes cities.country stores (ISO-2 on live data). NULL or empty = every country, which is the pre-column behaviour. Scopes sequence_auto_enrol_scraped, which is otherwise global and would spend the daily send cap on whichever country was scraped most recently. See dashboard/lib/sequences/autoEnrol.ts.';


--

--

COMMENT ON COLUMN public.app_settings.active_order_countries IS 'Working-set criterion: delivery-country allow-list (Shopify shipping country codes, e.g. ES, FR). Combines with active_order_tags via OR. Empty = no country criterion (see isInWorkingSet).';


--

--

COMMENT ON COLUMN public.app_settings.run_all_orders IS 'Explicit "run every order through the system" switch. true short-circuits active_order_tags/active_order_countries entirely. Default false — empty criteria must stay safe (no orders), never implicitly "all orders".';


--

--

COMMENT ON COLUMN public.app_settings.working_set_radius_km IS 'Search radius (km) from an order''s delivery coordinates used to decide whether the existing florist pool has usable candidates on working-set entry. Below this, ingest is requested instead of silently escalating (see ingest-worker/src/lateMatch.ts::matchAndWriteCandidates + db.ts::requestCandidateIngest). Default 5, editable in Settings.';


--

--

COMMENT ON COLUMN public.app_settings.offer_parallel_sends IS 'Maximum number of live sent/opened offers the wave engine may keep open per order in auto mode. 1 = sequential one-at-a-time funnel. Higher values send to multiple ranked candidates in parallel while still respecting offer expiry, accept CAS, max waves and refill/escalation guards.';


--

--

COMMENT ON COLUMN public.app_settings.payout_blocked_alert_extra_emails IS 'Recipients of the blocked-payout CX alert (live mode). The complete list — not added to anyone else.';


--

--

CREATE TABLE public.cities (
    id uuid DEFAULT gen_random_uuid() NOT NULL,
    country text NOT NULL,
    city text NOT NULL,
    center_lat double precision NOT NULL,
    center_lng double precision NOT NULL,
    radius_km double precision,
    region text DEFAULT ''::text NOT NULL,
    ingested_at timestamp with time zone DEFAULT now() NOT NULL,
    source text DEFAULT 'ingest'::text,
    CONSTRAINT cities_source_check CHECK ((source = ANY (ARRAY['ingest'::text, 'manual'::text])))
);



--

--

COMMENT ON COLUMN public.cities.source IS 'How this city row came to exist. ''ingest'' = created by an Apify scrape (the default, and true of every row predating this column). ''manual'' = created to hold a hand-added partner florist whose location no existing city covers; nothing has been scraped here, so ingested_at is a creation timestamp rather than a scrape time.';


--

--

CREATE TABLE public.client_comms (
    id uuid DEFAULT gen_random_uuid() NOT NULL,
    order_id uuid NOT NULL,
    kind text NOT NULL,
    sent_at timestamp with time zone DEFAULT now() NOT NULL,
    test_mode boolean NOT NULL,
    CONSTRAINT client_comms_kind_check CHECK ((kind = ANY (ARRAY['assigned'::text, 'on_the_way'::text, 'delivered'::text])))
);



--

--

CREATE TABLE public.communications (
    id uuid DEFAULT gen_random_uuid() NOT NULL,
    created_at timestamp with time zone DEFAULT now() NOT NULL,
    channel text NOT NULL,
    audience text NOT NULL,
    kind text NOT NULL,
    order_id uuid,
    florist_id uuid,
    assignment_id uuid,
    issue_id uuid,
    to_address text,
    subject text,
    body text,
    test_mode boolean NOT NULL,
    status text NOT NULL,
    provider text NOT NULL,
    provider_message_id text,
    error text,
    actor text,
    html text,
    rfc_message_id text,
    CONSTRAINT communications_audience_check CHECK ((audience = ANY (ARRAY['florist'::text, 'client'::text, 'cx'::text, 'staff'::text]))),
    CONSTRAINT communications_channel_check CHECK ((channel = ANY (ARRAY['email'::text, 'push'::text, 'sms'::text]))),
    CONSTRAINT communications_status_check CHECK ((status = ANY (ARRAY['sent'::text, 'failed'::text, 'skipped'::text, 'received'::text])))
);



--

--

COMMENT ON COLUMN public.communications.status IS 'sent | failed | skipped for outbound messages; received for an inbound reply from a florist (logged by lib/conversations.ts::ingestInbound, sender address in actor).';


--

--

COMMENT ON COLUMN public.communications.rfc_message_id IS 'The RFC 5322 Message-ID header we set on an outbound email, e.g. <fc.<uuid>@mail.fc.example.com>. Read back by lib/inboundMatch.ts from a reply''s In-Reply-To/References to recover order_id + florist_id. Distinct from provider_message_id, which is Resend''s own opaque id.';


--

--

CREATE TABLE public.content_translations (
    id uuid DEFAULT gen_random_uuid() NOT NULL,
    field text NOT NULL,
    source_hash text NOT NULL,
    locale text NOT NULL,
    value text NOT NULL,
    provider text NOT NULL,
    source_text text,
    created_at timestamp with time zone DEFAULT now() NOT NULL,
    CONSTRAINT content_translations_field_check CHECK ((field = ANY (ARRAY['title'::text, 'variant'::text, 'recipe'::text, 'components'::text, 'addons'::text]))),
    CONSTRAINT content_translations_provider_check CHECK ((provider = ANY (ARRAY['shopify'::text, 'llm'::text])))
);



--

--

CREATE TABLE public.conversation_messages (
    id uuid DEFAULT gen_random_uuid() NOT NULL,
    conversation_id uuid NOT NULL,
    direction text NOT NULL,
    channel text NOT NULL,
    from_address text,
    to_address text,
    subject text,
    body_text text,
    body_html text,
    provider text,
    provider_message_id text,
    provider_event_id text,
    communication_id uuid,
    ai_generated boolean DEFAULT false NOT NULL,
    ai_model text,
    ai_confidence numeric,
    ai_intent text,
    ai_escalate boolean,
    ai_raw jsonb,
    status text DEFAULT 'sent'::text NOT NULL,
    suppress_reason text,
    actor text,
    created_at timestamp with time zone DEFAULT now() NOT NULL,
    CONSTRAINT conversation_messages_channel_check CHECK ((channel = ANY (ARRAY['email'::text, 'sms'::text, 'app'::text]))),
    CONSTRAINT conversation_messages_direction_check CHECK ((direction = ANY (ARRAY['in'::text, 'out'::text]))),
    CONSTRAINT conversation_messages_status_check CHECK ((status = ANY (ARRAY['received'::text, 'draft'::text, 'sent'::text, 'suppressed'::text])))
);



--

--

COMMENT ON COLUMN public.conversation_messages.ai_raw IS 'The full structured response from the model. Kept so an escalation can be audited afterwards — "why did it think that" is unanswerable from a confidence score alone.';


--

--

COMMENT ON COLUMN public.conversation_messages.status IS 'draft = the model wrote it and the escalation gate refused to auto-send; a human approves or edits it. suppressed = we deliberately did not answer (a hard opt-out, an auto-responder, a bounce) and the model never saw the message at all.';


--

--

CREATE TABLE public.conversations (
    id uuid DEFAULT gen_random_uuid() NOT NULL,
    florist_id uuid,
    channel text NOT NULL,
    persona_id uuid,
    enrolment_id uuid,
    subject text,
    status text DEFAULT 'bot'::text NOT NULL,
    auto_turns integer DEFAULT 0 NOT NULL,
    last_inbound_at timestamp with time zone,
    last_outbound_at timestamp with time zone,
    escalated_at timestamp with time zone,
    escalation_reason text,
    cx_unread boolean DEFAULT false NOT NULL,
    created_at timestamp with time zone DEFAULT now() NOT NULL,
    updated_at timestamp with time zone DEFAULT now() NOT NULL,
    order_id uuid,
    assignment_id uuid,
    kind text DEFAULT 'recruiting'::text NOT NULL,
    florist_unread boolean DEFAULT false NOT NULL,
    ai_disclosed_at timestamp with time zone,
    CONSTRAINT conversations_channel_check CHECK ((channel = ANY (ARRAY['email'::text, 'sms'::text, 'app'::text]))),
    CONSTRAINT conversations_kind_check CHECK ((kind = ANY (ARRAY['recruiting'::text, 'support'::text]))),
    CONSTRAINT conversations_status_check CHECK ((status = ANY (ARRAY['bot'::text, 'awaiting_human'::text, 'closed'::text])))
);



--

--

COMMENT ON COLUMN public.conversations.order_id IS 'Set by lib/inboundMatch.ts (reply-address token, then In-Reply-To threading) or directly when the thread is opened from an order in the florist app. NEVER inferred from subject or body text: attaching one florist''s message to another order is worse than leaving it unattached, so an unmatched inbound lands here as null and goes to a human.';


--

--

COMMENT ON COLUMN public.conversations.kind IS 'recruiting = a prospect being signed; the agent may state only lib/cxAgent.ts::APPROVED_FACTS. support = a joined florist asking about their own order; the agent may state only the facts lib/supportFacts.ts computed for THIS conversation, enforced by lib/cxAgentGuard.ts::moneyClaimOutsideFacts. Adding a kind means adding a fact set — an agent with no allowed facts can say nothing at all, which is the correct failure direction.';


--

--

COMMENT ON COLUMN public.conversations.ai_disclosed_at IS 'When the AI disclosure was first sent in this thread (EU AI Act Art. 50). Set by lib/conversations.ts on the first model-written reply; the disclosure line itself is email.disclosure.proactive in the i18n catalog.';


--

--

CREATE TABLE public.country_keywords (
    country text NOT NULL,
    keywords jsonb NOT NULL,
    language text,
    updated_at timestamp with time zone DEFAULT now() NOT NULL
);



--

--

CREATE TABLE public.delivery_events (
    id uuid DEFAULT gen_random_uuid() NOT NULL,
    assignment_id uuid NOT NULL,
    type text NOT NULL,
    photo_key text,
    note text,
    created_at timestamp with time zone DEFAULT now() NOT NULL
);



--

--

CREATE TABLE public.email_events (
    id uuid DEFAULT gen_random_uuid() NOT NULL,
    communication_id uuid,
    event_type text NOT NULL,
    occurred_at timestamp with time zone DEFAULT now() NOT NULL,
    raw jsonb NOT NULL,
    provider_event_id text NOT NULL,
    CONSTRAINT email_events_event_type_check CHECK ((event_type = ANY (ARRAY['delivered'::text, 'opened'::text, 'clicked'::text, 'bounced'::text, 'complained'::text])))
);



--

--

COMMENT ON COLUMN public.email_events.provider_event_id IS 'Svix message id (svix-id header) of the webhook delivery that produced this row. Unique: the webhook inserts on conflict do nothing so provider retries are idempotent.';


--

--

CREATE TABLE public.external_ops (
    id uuid DEFAULT gen_random_uuid() NOT NULL,
    provider text NOT NULL,
    operation text NOT NULL,
    direction text DEFAULT 'out'::text NOT NULL,
    order_id uuid,
    ref text,
    ok boolean,
    skipped boolean DEFAULT false NOT NULL,
    status_code integer,
    duration_ms integer,
    error text,
    meta jsonb,
    created_at timestamp with time zone DEFAULT now() NOT NULL,
    CONSTRAINT external_ops_direction_check CHECK ((direction = ANY (ARRAY['in'::text, 'out'::text])))
);



--

--

CREATE TABLE public.florist_invites (
    id uuid DEFAULT gen_random_uuid() NOT NULL,
    florist_id uuid NOT NULL,
    email text NOT NULL,
    token text NOT NULL,
    invited_by text NOT NULL,
    created_at timestamp with time zone DEFAULT now() NOT NULL,
    expires_at timestamp with time zone DEFAULT (now() + '7 days'::interval) NOT NULL,
    accepted_at timestamp with time zone
);



--

--

CREATE TABLE public.florist_magic_tokens (
    token text NOT NULL,
    florist_id uuid NOT NULL,
    dest text NOT NULL,
    purpose text NOT NULL,
    assignment_id uuid,
    expires_at timestamp with time zone NOT NULL,
    created_at timestamp with time zone DEFAULT now() NOT NULL,
    last_used_at timestamp with time zone,
    use_count integer DEFAULT 0 NOT NULL,
    revoked_at timestamp with time zone
);



--

--

COMMENT ON TABLE public.florist_magic_tokens IS 'One-per-send sign-in tokens for florist-facing email/SMS links. Reusable within a 30-day window (lib/floristMagicLink.ts::MAGIC_TOKEN_TTL_DAYS) — deliberately NOT single-use, because corporate link scanners (Outlook Safe Links) and Gmail''s prefetcher follow URLs before the human clicks and would burn a single-use token on a valid email.';


--

--

COMMENT ON COLUMN public.florist_magic_tokens.dest IS 'Relative destination path (e.g. /florist/orders/<assignment_id>). Stored on the row rather than passed in the URL so the emailed link carries no redirect parameter to tamper with; the redeem route re-validates it via isSafeDest before redirecting.';


--

--

COMMENT ON COLUMN public.florist_magic_tokens.purpose IS 'offer | issue | onboarding — which message minted it. Diagnostic only; the redeem route does not branch on it.';


--

--

COMMENT ON COLUMN public.florist_magic_tokens.assignment_id IS 'Set for offer/issue tokens so a single order''s links can be revoked together. ON DELETE SET NULL: losing the assignment must not silently delete an audit row.';


--

--

COMMENT ON COLUMN public.florist_magic_tokens.use_count IS 'Bumped on each successful redeem. A count far above 1 is the signal that a link was forwarded or shared.';


--

--

COMMENT ON COLUMN public.florist_magic_tokens.revoked_at IS 'Manual kill switch for one send, without locking the florist out of every other link they hold.';


--

--

CREATE TABLE public.florist_meetings (
    id uuid DEFAULT gen_random_uuid() NOT NULL,
    florist_id uuid NOT NULL,
    title text,
    meeting_at timestamp with time zone NOT NULL,
    outcome text,
    next_follow_up_at timestamp with time zone,
    created_by text,
    created_at timestamp with time zone DEFAULT now() NOT NULL
);



--

--

CREATE TABLE public.florist_messages (
    id uuid DEFAULT gen_random_uuid() NOT NULL,
    florist_id uuid NOT NULL,
    kind text NOT NULL,
    florist_unread boolean DEFAULT true NOT NULL,
    created_at timestamp with time zone DEFAULT now() NOT NULL,
    read_at timestamp with time zone,
    CONSTRAINT florist_messages_kind_check CHECK ((kind = 'welcome'::text))
);



--

--

COMMENT ON TABLE public.florist_messages IS 'Messages addressed to a florist rather than to an order (welcome note, and later any broadcast notice). Body/title are NOT stored — `kind` selects an i18n catalog entry rendered at read time, so the copy stays translated and stays editable from /email-templates. Contrast order_issues, which is always about one order.';


--

--

CREATE TABLE public.florist_networks (
    id uuid DEFAULT gen_random_uuid() NOT NULL,
    name text NOT NULL,
    domain text NOT NULL,
    kind text NOT NULL,
    contact_email text,
    notes text,
    created_at timestamp with time zone DEFAULT now() NOT NULL,
    CONSTRAINT florist_networks_kind_check CHECK ((kind = ANY (ARRAY['network'::text, 'franchise'::text, 'chain'::text, 'directory'::text])))
);



--

--

COMMENT ON TABLE public.florist_networks IS 'Florist networks, franchises, chains and directories whose site hosts member shops. A florist linked to one has a website_url that is not its own site, so its scraped email is the network''s, not the shop''s.';


--

--

CREATE TABLE public.florist_notes (
    id uuid DEFAULT gen_random_uuid() NOT NULL,
    florist_id uuid NOT NULL,
    author text,
    body text NOT NULL,
    created_at timestamp with time zone DEFAULT now() NOT NULL
);



--

--

CREATE SEQUENCE public.florist_number_seq
    START WITH 9000000
    INCREMENT BY 1
    MINVALUE 9000000
    NO MAXVALUE
    CACHE 1;



--

--

CREATE TABLE public.florists (
    id uuid DEFAULT gen_random_uuid() NOT NULL,
    city_id uuid NOT NULL,
    place_id text NOT NULL,
    name text NOT NULL,
    address text,
    lat double precision,
    lng double precision,
    rating double precision,
    review_count integer,
    distance_km_from_center double precision,
    phone_maps text,
    website_url text,
    has_website boolean DEFAULT false NOT NULL,
    is_ecommerce boolean,
    ecommerce_signals jsonb,
    email text,
    phone_web text,
    owner_name text,
    shop_highlight text,
    enrichment_notes text,
    drafted_email text,
    order_sms_opt_out boolean DEFAULT false NOT NULL,
    order_sms_snoozed_until timestamp with time zone,
    drafted_sms text,
    ingested_at timestamp with time zone DEFAULT now() NOT NULL,
    deleted_at timestamp with time zone,
    excluded_at timestamp with time zone,
    lifecycle_stage text DEFAULT 'found'::text NOT NULL,
    source text DEFAULT 'new'::text,
    source_notes text,
    exclusion_reason text,
    delivery_radius_km double precision,
    business_hours jsonb,
    capacity_per_day integer,
    payout_terms text,
    whatsapp text,
    preferred_channel text,
    trust_tier text DEFAULT '2'::text,
    onboarded_at timestamp with time zone,
    airwallex_payout_ref text,
    locale text,
    order_emails_snoozed_until timestamp with time zone,
    order_emails_opt_out boolean DEFAULT false NOT NULL,
    unsubscribe_token text,
    join_token text,
    join_token_expires_at timestamp with time zone,
    joined_at timestamp with time zone,
    next_day_cutoff_hour integer,
    category_name text,
    categories jsonb,
    phone_mobile text,
    shop_story text,
    is_test_shop boolean DEFAULT false NOT NULL,
    network_id uuid,
    email_shared_count integer DEFAULT 1 NOT NULL,
    email_bounced_at timestamp with time zone,
    provisional_activated_at timestamp with time zone,
    provisional_source text,
    added_by text,
    sms_undeliverable_at timestamp with time zone,
    florist_number integer,
    data_issues text[] DEFAULT '{}'::text[] NOT NULL,
    data_issues_seen_at timestamp with time zone,
    data_issues_last_order_id uuid,
    data_issues_skip_count integer DEFAULT 0 NOT NULL,
    CONSTRAINT florists_lifecycle_stage_check CHECK ((lifecycle_stage = ANY (ARRAY['found'::text, 'targeted'::text, 'contacted'::text, 'engaged'::text, 'onboarding'::text, 'production'::text, 'lost'::text]))),
    CONSTRAINT florists_next_day_cutoff_hour_check CHECK (((next_day_cutoff_hour IS NULL) OR (next_day_cutoff_hour = ANY (ARRAY[11, 12, 13, 14, 15])))),
    CONSTRAINT florists_preferred_channel_check CHECK ((preferred_channel = ANY (ARRAY['email'::text, 'whatsapp'::text, 'app'::text]))),
    CONSTRAINT florists_source_check CHECK ((source = ANY (ARRAY['existing'::text, 'known'::text, 'new'::text]))),
    CONSTRAINT florists_trust_tier_check CHECK ((trust_tier = ANY (ARRAY['1'::text, '2'::text, '3'::text, '4'::text, '5'::text])))
);



--

--

COMMENT ON COLUMN public.florists.order_sms_opt_out IS 'Permanent opt-out from order-offer SMS, set from /florist/unsubscribe/[token]. Independent of order_emails_opt_out.';


--

--

COMMENT ON COLUMN public.florists.order_sms_snoozed_until IS 'Temporary (30-day) snooze from order-offer SMS. Independent of order_emails_snoozed_until.';


--

--

COMMENT ON COLUMN public.florists.drafted_sms IS 'Generated recruiting-outreach SMS draft (dashboard/lib/draftSms.ts). Short plain text, no subject — the SMS sibling of drafted_email.';


--

--

COMMENT ON COLUMN public.florists.order_emails_snoozed_until IS 'Florist self-service "pause 30 days" (dashboard/app/florist/unsubscribe). Null = not snoozed; a future timestamp = order-offer emails suppressed until then (auto-resumes, no cron needed). Checked in dashboard/lib/reachoutSend.ts::sendOffer.';


--

--

COMMENT ON COLUMN public.florists.order_emails_opt_out IS 'Florist self-service "stop completely" (dashboard/app/florist/unsubscribe). Permanent — no self-service re-opt-in; staff can clear it directly in the DB if a florist asks to come back. Checked in dashboard/lib/reachoutSend.ts::sendOffer.';


--

--

COMMENT ON COLUMN public.florists.unsubscribe_token IS 'Opaque token for the no-login unsubscribe link in the offer email footer. Generated lazily on first offer send (dashboard/lib/reachoutSend.ts::sendOffer), never backfilled.';


--

--

COMMENT ON COLUMN public.florists.join_token IS 'Opaque token for the no-login "join our network" link (dashboard/app/florist/accept). Minted lazily by app/api/florists/draft-email when a recruiting draft is generated, via lib/floristJoin.ts::needsNewJoinToken.';


--

--

COMMENT ON COLUMN public.florists.join_token_expires_at IS '30 days from mint (lib/floristJoin.ts::joinTokenExpiry). A live recruiting-draft regeneration refreshes it once expired.';


--

--

COMMENT ON COLUMN public.florists.joined_at IS 'Set by app/api/florist/accept on successful self-registration. Null = not yet joined; non-null makes the accept link idempotent (read-only confirmation instead of the form).';


--

--

COMMENT ON COLUMN public.florists.next_day_cutoff_hour IS 'Florist-set next-day-delivery order cutoff, one of 11/12/13/14/15. Null until the florist submits the accept form.';


--

--

COMMENT ON COLUMN public.florists.category_name IS 'Google Maps'' primary category for this place (Apify `categoryName`, e.g. "Florist"). Captured by ingest/scrape.py::normalize_item. Null for rows scraped before 2026-08-04, and for places Google gives no category.';


--

--

COMMENT ON COLUMN public.florists.categories IS 'The full list of categories Google assigned (Apify `categories`, e.g. ["Florist","Gift shop"]). Together with category_name this is the input to the relevance filter''s free rule (relevance.py::category_matches_florist) — persisted so an existing florist can be re-judged without re-scraping.';


--

--

COMMENT ON COLUMN public.florists.phone_mobile IS 'Florist-confirmed mobile for order alerts, normalised to E.164 at write time by the join form (dashboard/app/api/florist/accept). Preferred over phone_web and phone_maps by lib/phone.ts::resolveFloristSmsPhone. Null for every florist who has not self-registered.';


--

--

COMMENT ON COLUMN public.florists.shop_story IS 'Free text the florist wrote about their own shop on the join form (600 char cap, enforced in lib/floristAccept.ts). Distinct from shop_highlight, which is LLM-researched by the ingest pipeline.';


--

--

COMMENT ON COLUMN public.florists.is_test_shop IS 'A florist WE own, used to exercise the real order loop. While app_settings.test_mode is on, these receive real email/SMS at their real address with working magic links; every other florist gets the test inbox and inert placeholder tokens. Also governs automatic matching via app_settings.test_shop_matching.';


--

--

COMMENT ON COLUMN public.florists.network_id IS 'The network/franchise/chain/directory whose site this florist''s website_url points at. Non-null means `email` is the network''s address, not the shop''s: the offer email leg is skipped and the offer hedges to SMS + push.';


--

--

COMMENT ON COLUMN public.florists.email_shared_count IS 'Number of florist rows holding this exact email. >1 means the address cannot identify this shop; the offer email leg is skipped. Maintained by the shared-address sweep (ingest/networks.py::sweep_shared_emails).';


--

--

COMMENT ON COLUMN public.florists.email_bounced_at IS 'When this florist''s address hard-bounced, per the Resend webhook. Non-null skips the offer email leg (SMS + push still fire). Cleared when the address is corrected.';


--

--

COMMENT ON COLUMN public.florists.provisional_activated_at IS 'Set by lib/coldOffer.ts::buildProvisionalActivation when a cold-offer shop accepts. It fills in delivery_radius_km and trust_tier — exactly the two things lib/floristActivation.ts::computeActivation and ingest-worker/src/match.ts::passesHardFilter demand. Note the distinction: the activation gate is NOT bypassed, its inputs are supplied. No new code path can offer to a shop that fails the filter.';


--

--

COMMENT ON COLUMN public.florists.added_by IS 'Staff email of whoever created this florist by hand (app/api/florists/create). Null for every ingest-created row, which is all of them before 2026-08-12.';


--

--

COMMENT ON COLUMN public.florists.sms_undeliverable_at IS 'When Telnyx last reported a PERMANENT delivery failure for this florist''s number (see app/api/webhooks/telnyx/route.ts for the error codes that count). Non-null skips the offer SMS leg; email + push still fire. Cleared when the number is corrected.';


--

--

COMMENT ON COLUMN public.florists.florist_number IS 'Facundo-minted Florist ID (7-digit integer), assigned per-shop by staff via assign_florist_number() for florists that never had one; a known florist''s real existing id is entered by hand instead (staff-editable either way). Written back to Shopify under the "Tookan Florist Id" metafield (custom.tookan_florist_id) — confirmed live 2026-08-21; NOT "Odoo Florist Order Id" (custom.odoo_florist_order_id), which real order data shows tracks the ORDER, not the florist. See dashboard/lib/shopifyWriteback.ts for the our-name -> Shopify-name mapping and dashboard/lib/floristNumber.ts for the reserved-range constant (must move together with this sequence''s start value).';


--

--

COMMENT ON COLUMN public.florists.data_issues IS 'Why an automatic order offer cannot usefully reach this shop: any of missing-email, bad-email, shared-email, missing-location. Always empty for a shop that has signed up (onboarding/production). Maintained by trigger florists_data_issues_sync from florist_data_issues(); never write it directly. Shops with a non-empty value are kept out of order candidate lists (dashboard/lib/match.ts::contactGaps).';


--

--

COMMENT ON COLUMN public.florists.data_issues_seen_at IS 'Last time the matcher left this shop out of a real order because of data_issues. Null = never left out of one.';


--

--

COMMENT ON COLUMN public.florists.data_issues_last_order_id IS 'The order this shop was most recently left out of because of data_issues.';


--

--

COMMENT ON COLUMN public.florists.data_issues_skip_count IS 'How many orders this shop has been left out of because of data_issues. Counted once per order, not once per matching run.';


